WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.330
A new model came out this morning.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.670
By lunch, someone online says it changes everything.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.210
But will it change anything for your work?

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.790
Many people never choose at all.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.470
They use the default.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.670
And when people compare, they see the names.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.290
It's like judging a wine by its price tag.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.510
That's why a taste test hides the labels.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:29.650
You give two or more options the same request, and pick the one you'd use.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.590
You decide what good looks like first,

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.300
because afterward, you're only explaining a choice.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:43.160
So in this adventure, built for more advanced users, you get a method to build your personal benchmark:

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:49.500
a task set that represents how you work, and a routing card for which option does which task.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:54.700
Then every new model, tool or feature gets the same objective test,

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.780
and you decide whether it joins your roster.
